Proposed Extraction & Distribution Process
1. Standardized Research Output Format
Each research document in the Research/ folder should follow a consistent structure that aligns with EPIS-COMPASS and makes extraction systematic:

# Research Document
- Research Question
- System Map
- Evidence (with OBSERVED/INFERRED/HYPOTHESIZED labels)
- Mechanisms
- Failure Modes
- Real-World Practice
- Open Questions
- Practical Experiments
- Epistemic Update
2. Extraction Protocol
A systematic process for analyzing research documents:

Phase 1: Pass Extraction

Read research document once to identify all Atlas-relevant nodes
Tag each finding with: category, evidence quality, epistemic status
Extract: new nodes, reinforced nodes, relationships, contradictions, anomalies
Phase 2: Validation

Cross-reference with existing Category nodes to avoid duplicates
Assess evidence quality (primary source vs inference)
Mark hypothesized nodes for future validation
Phase 3: Relationship Mapping

Identify connections between nodes (e.g., "technology X enables capability Y")
Note contradictions and anomalies explicitly
Map constraints to problems/workflows they affect
3. Distribution Protocol
Rules for moving extracted nodes to Categories:

Node Creation

Each node gets its own markdown file in the appropriate Category folder
Standard node metadata: source document, extraction date, evidence quality, epistemic status
Include back-reference to original research document
Node Structure

---
category: [Category Name]
source: [Research Document Name]
extracted: [Date]
evidence_quality: [HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW]
epistemic_status: [OBSERVED/INFERRED/HYPOTHESIZED]
related_nodes: [list of related node files]
---
 
# [Node Title]
 
## What it is
[Description]
 
## Evidence
[Source material with citations]
 
## Relationships
[Connections to other nodes]
 
## Contradictions/Anomalies
[If applicable]
 
## Follow-up Research Needed
[If applicable]
4. Quality Control Gates
Gate 1: Research completeness (follows EPIS-COMPASS structure)
Gate 2: Extraction completeness (all 8 extraction items addressed)
Gate 3: Distribution accuracy (nodes properly categorized and formatted)
Gate 4: Consistency check (no duplicate nodes, relationships maintained)
5. Traceability System
Every Category node must reference its source Research document
Research documents should have an "Extraction Log" section tracking what was extracted and where
Use Obsidian's link system for bidirectional references
6. Role Definitions
Define who performs each step:

Researcher: Produces research following EPIS-COMPASS
Extractor: Systematically extracts nodes following Extraction Protocol
Distributor: Creates/updates Category nodes following Distribution Protocol
Validator: Performs quality control gates

7. Process Workflow
Research (follows EPIS-COMPASS)
    ↓
Extraction (systematic node identification)
    ↓
Validation (quality gates)
    ↓
Distribution (node creation in Categories)
    ↓
Cross-reference (relationship mapping)
    ↓
Atlas Update (contradiction/anomaly synthesis)